<title>UK: Thomas Cook wins new HK airport contract.</title>
<headline>Thomas Cook wins new HK airport contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Travel agent Thomas Cook said it won an exclusive deal to provide retail foreign exchange services at Hong Kong's new Chek Lap Kok airport, due to open next year.</p>
<p>Thomas Cook said it won the 4-1/2 year contract to operate all 12 retail foreign exchange locations at the Hong Kong Sky Mall.</p>
<p>The company, majority owned by Germany's Westdeutsche Landesbank Girozentrale, will hold a 75-percent stake in a venture that will manage the business.</p>
<p>The remaining 25 percent stake will be owned by Hong Kong's Sun Hung Kai Properties Ltd.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
